<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="40925" href="schedule/2005/fall/ARTH/591/40925.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2005" href="schedule/2005.xml">2005</calendarYear><term id="120058" href="schedule/2005/fall.xml">Fall 2005</term><subject id="ARTH" href="schedule/2005/fall/ARTH.xml">Art--History</subject><course id="591" href="schedule/2005/fall/ARTH/591.xml">Individual Readings</course></parents><sectionNumber>A  </sectionNumber><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Topic: Modern and Contemporary African Art.  This seminar will explore the predicament of "modern" and "contemporary" client-driven African art from the 1960s to the present. We shall discuss the inevitable issues of marginalizations; the Western perceptions of "Africanness" and "authenticity," as well as charged and contested tags of "traditional," "modern," "urban," "international," and "contemporary."</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2005-08-24Z</startDate><endDate>2005-12-09Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="CNF">Conference</type><start>03:00 PM</start><end>05:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>W      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>236</roomNumber><buildingName>Art and Design Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Rush" firstName="D">Rush, D</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>